== SOURCE
l:Y_ := { f_ -> f_ l:Y_ 'f_ }
== TITLE
Y, the Sage Bird: recursion
== NOTE f_
The step
A function that is handed the whole recursive function and makes one step with it.
== NOTE l:Y_ #2
Y itself
The library's own name, used in its body: Y calls itself.
== NOTE 'f_
Quoted
The quote passes f as a value instead of applying it.
== NOTE f_ l:Y_ 'f_
Y f is f (Y f)
f is handed Y f. That does not loop forever because f's parameter is lazy (`~`), used only when needed. APL has no such operator: a dfn recurses with `∇`.
